cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its execution evidence, please cite this work."
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yygotm/gilbreath-verification"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23160565"
title: "A Reproducible CPU Verification of Gilbreath's Conjecture up to 10^13"
authors:
  - family-names: "Shimizu"
    given-names: "Hirotaka"
abstract: >-
  A CPU implementation and execution evidence for a finite verification of
  Gilbreath's conjecture covering prime positions below 10^13, yielding
  pi(10^13) = 346065536839 and G = 635. Includes source, tests, segment logs,
  reproduction instructions, and checksums. The result agrees with the
  established value and does not claim a new numerical record. Research and
  original computation were performed on Intel hardware; archived full-range
  logs are from a subsequent AMD reproduction check. The work was carried out
  by Hirotaka Shimizu with assistance from Claude and OpenAI Codex.
keywords:
  - Gilbreath conjecture
  - computational number theory
  - reproducibility
  - prime numbers
